  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-forensic art direction, disciplined cyan/red semantics, crisp borders, and a clear hero-to-evidence hierarchy. Desktop feels polished, but the oversized headline leaves substantial dead space and competes with the dense evidence panel. Tablet/mobile headline wrapping is awkward, the tiny monospaced metadata strains readability, and the mobile chart labels are nearly illegible. The responsive header also feels visually incomplete: navigation is clipped into a horizontal rail, while mobile drops the brand name and red-mode control.",
    "fix": "Tighten desktop hero proportions, tune responsive headline size/measure for cleaner breaks, enlarge chart and metadata text on mobile, and redesign the compact header with a clear active item plus deliberate menu affordance instead of visibly clipped navigation.",
